{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>A remnant is left. And desolation.</b> A noun from the root of שואה (Isaiah 10:3):" "And the prophet said 'a remnant is left' in the manner of human speech, so that the hearers may understand; and likewise, 'better than both of them' (Ecclesiastes 4:3):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra parses the word נשאר in the verse; the second lemma 'ושאייה' refers to a related form he discusses.", 1 "The Ecclesiastes citation appears to illustrate anthropopathic or accommodated language directed at human understanding."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:56.900496672Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}